# Ownership, and - as the ruleset now stands - a gate. This requests review
# automatically and makes the boundary visible in the diff view, and because
# Required approvals is 1, "Require review from Code Owners" is enforced: a pull
# request touching these paths needs an approval from the owner named below.
#
# That enforcement rests entirely on the number. At Required approvals 0, GitHub
# does not enforce the code-owner requirement at all, while the tick box next to
# it looks exactly the same - observed here on five pull requests, every one
# reporting an empty reviewDecision. Nothing in CI reports the difference. So
# the number must not go back to 0: doing so silently removes this gate and
# leaves a settings page that still reads as configured. The setting itself is
# written down in docs/repository-setup.md, which says to re-read that number.
#
# The hard refusal of these paths does not depend on any of it: it is the
# `Repository policy` check.
#
# Patterns without a slash match at any depth, so a skill added at a different
# nesting level is still covered.

*                       @brunocats
SKILL.md                @brunocats
evals/                  @brunocats
/AGENTS.md              @brunocats
/.github/               @brunocats
